# Ship quality

Before implementing: re-read the skills, rules, moat, and docs that apply. If the request is not aligned, **stop and ask**.

After implementing: iterate until one next step is obvious, then prove it.

```bash
npm test
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm run build
```

Then smoke the changed screens. `npm run check` is the fast lint+test+typecheck loop — still build and smoke before you stop.

After a user-facing phase, the last message must include a founder retest script: already proven, numbered clicks, expected screens, not-yet, and when we can move on.

Do not add a dependency, cartoon icons, or a Year-1 ban to “make it nicer.” Lucide strokes already in the repo are the icon language. See skill `kirabaki-ship-quality`.
